ty if <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text=
-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">=
status</code> is equal to "success"? Can you have some <code class=3D"bg-te=
xt-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre=
-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">data</code> <em>and</em> a=
n <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-dan=
ger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">erro=
r</code> at the same time? We just don't know!
With a <strong>union type</strong>, it's a different story:
